{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Allow the sale of Canada goose meat in the UK",
        "additional_details": "We ask the public to back British farming, and we want to help support British farmers. Research suggests about 3 Canada geese eat as much as one sheep. Canada geese are already a legal quarry species, controlled under licence year-round, yet unlike woodpigeon, their meat cannot be sold.\r\n\r\nPermitting the licensed, traceable sale of Canada geese through approved game dealers could help farmers recover financial losses they may have experienced, cut any waste and put lean, iron-rich UK-sourced meat in schools, hospitals and prisons across the country.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to allow the sale of Canada goose meat in the UK for food all year, under licence. These birds are already legally controlled to protect farmers\u2019 grazing. Permitting their sale could supply lean, local protein to schools, hospitals and prisons, instead of being wasted.",
